    "source": {
      "goCharacterKey": "Yanfei",
      "note": "Generated from Genshin Optimizer sheets (master) + allStat_gen skillParam. Hit keys match GO target paths; multKey = <hitKey>_mult. Levels: Lv10, except constellation-boosted talents of 4-star characters at Lv13 (C6 assumed). Normal/charged/plunging default to physical unless the sheet overrides the element (infusions are NOT applied). 2026-08-07: A4 Blazing Eye added as its own rotation target passive2/dmg (ATK x 80%, Pyro, counted as Charged Attack DMG so it takes charged_dmg_/pyro_dmg_ and her C2 charged CRIT Rate). It is a separate damage instance that fires only when a Charged Attack CRITs, so the hit def carries triggerCritRateScaled and the evaluator multiplies it by the capped crit rate under avgHit — GO models it identically as passive2.probabilistic_dmg. This replaces the old a4BlazingEye conditional, which folded charged_dmgIncFromAtk_ 0.8 into every Charged Attack hit: that both ignored the CRIT requirement and multiplied the proc by the CA target's rotation weight. 2026-08-08: the hit was originally keyed passive2/dmg, which broke the file's own \"hit keys match GO target paths\" rule — every hand-authored rotation copies GO and says passive2/probabilistic_dmg, and resolve_hit_definition exact-matches a character's own keys, so those targets silently scored 0. probabilistic_dmg is now the canonical key; passive2/dmg is kept as an alias so any rotation drafted against the old spelling still resolves.",
      "assumptions": {
        "constellation": 6,
        "characterLevel": 90,
        "autoTalentLevel": 10,
        "skillTalentLevel": 13,
        "burstTalentLevel": 13
      }
    }
  },
